{#
    What is wrong with the step just submitted, each error linking to its field (#33).

    The form is novalidate and long — the actions step can run to fifty lines — so an
    error far down the page was easy to miss. Each item names the field and links to its
    input's id; following the link moves focus there. An error on a group (the list of
    actions, a whole line) has no single field to point at and is listed without a link.

    The box is the only role="alert" on the page: the per-field messages would talk over
    each other if each announced itself. The error-summary controller focuses it on load;
    without JavaScript the links still work.
#}

{% macro items(form, prefix = '') %}
    {%- set prefix = 'action_draft' in form.vars.block_prefixes
        ? 'Action ' ~ (form.vars.name + 1) ~ ' — '
        : prefix -%}
    {%- set label = form.vars.label is not empty ? form.vars.label|trans : null -%}
    {%- for error in form.vars.errors ?? [] -%}
        <li>
            {%- if form.vars.compound ?? false -%}
                {{ prefix }}{{ error.message }}
            {%- else -%}
                <a href="#{{ form.vars.id }}">{{ prefix }}{{ label ? label ~ ' : ' }}{{ error.message }}</a>
            {%- endif -%}
        </li>
    {%- endfor -%}
    {%- for child in form.children -%}
        {{ _self.items(child, prefix) }}
    {%- endfor -%}
{% endmacro %}

{% set items = _self.items(form) %}
{% set count = items|split('<li>')|length - 1 %}

<div class="alert alert--danger error-summary" role="alert" tabindex="-1" {{ stimulus_controller('error-summary') }}>
    <p class="alert__title">
        {{ count > 1 ? count ~ ' points à corriger' : 'Un point à corriger' }} avant de continuer.
    </p>
    <ul class="error-summary__list">{{ items }}</ul>
</div>
